// ASYNC_PLAN.md A4: what `async_ngl` and `await_fr` compile to.
//
// `await_fr` is one byte with no operands -- what is being awaited is
// whatever the expression under it left on the stack, and the opcode replaces
// it with what it settles to.
//
// `async_ngl` emits no code at all. It is a *flag on the proto*, which the
// disassembler prints in the header: calling the closure is what makes a task
// and returns an `otw`, and that decision belongs to the runtime, not to a
// different instruction sequence.
async_ngl bet twice(n) {
    bounce n * 2
}

bet plain(n) {
    bounce n * 2
}

yo p = twice(21)
yap await_fr p
yap await_fr twice(1) + await_fr twice(2)
